        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate bulkFollowUp Response"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_BULKFOLLOWUP_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1770618587977",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770618587979_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Absences: {{JSON.parse($context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAction).Absences}}\nExpenseReports: {{JSON.parse($context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAction).ExpenseReports}}\nbulkEmailSent: {{$context.$variables.bulkEmailSent}}\n\n- Outputs only the final message text based on Absences and ExpenseReports inputs, with four conditional cases. \n- Do not include Absences and Expense Report IDs in the output.\n\n- Case 1: Absences and ExpenseReports are non-empty\n  - If bulkEmailSent is true:\n    - Follow-up on ExpenseReports(<Expense Report IDs>) and Absence Requests(<Absence Report Types>) are sent to {{$context.$nodes.GETMGREMAIL.$output.items[0].DisplayName}}.\n  - If bulkEmailSent is false:\n    - Follow-up not sent for ExpenseReports(<Expense Report IDs>) and Absence Requests(<Absence Report Types>) because the manager could not be identified.\n\n- Case 2: Only Absences are non-empty\n  - If bulkEmailSent is true:\n    - Follow-up on Absence Requests(<Absence Report Types>) is sent to {{$context.$nodes.GETMGREMAIL.$output.items[0].DisplayName}}.\n  - If bulkEmailSent is false:\n    - Follow-up not sent for Absence Requests(<Absence Report Types>) because the manager could not be identified.\n\n- Case 3: Only ExpenseReports are non-empty\n  - If bulkEmailSent is true:\n    - Follow-up on ExpenseReports(<Expense Report IDs>) is sent to {{$context.$nodes.GETMGREMAIL.$output.items[0].DisplayName}}.\n  - If bulkEmailSent is false:\n    - Follow-up not sent for ExpenseReports(<Expense Report IDs>) because the manager could not be identified.\n\n- Case 4: All empty\n  - No pending Absence Requests or ExpenseReports require follow-up at this time.\n\n### OUTPUT_FORMAT (STRICT)\n- If {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.locale}} exists,\n  - Must Generate the output in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.locale}} language."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "### Sorting Rule\nOrder results by priority level:\n- `alert`\n- `warning`\n- `default`\n\nReturn only the final 5 items.\n\n### Output format (STRICT)\n- **Must** generate the entire data in XML block(except links and SRNumbers) in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.locale}} language."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate initDisplay"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_INITDISPLAY",
          "id": "1770620341864",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770620341865_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Input Data\n{{$context.$nodes.GENERATERESPONSE.$output}}\n\n### Instructions\nYou are a specialized UI rendering assistant. You must adhere to the standard oraInfoDisplay Knowledge Base.\n\n**DIRECTIVE:** Your sole purpose is to transform input data into a valid `oraInfoDisplay` XML block using the `messageListWidget`.\n\n### OUTPUT_FORMAT (STRICT)\n- If {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.locale}} exists,\n  - **Must** translate the entire XML block(except links and SRNumbers) to {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.locale}} language."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "GenerateResponse"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770216082569"
          },
          "code": "GENERATERESPONSE",
          "id": "1770620950986",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770620950987_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Data\n- `SRs`: {{$context.$nodes.GETSERVICEREQUEST.$output}}\n- `Absences`: {{$context.$nodes.GETABSENCE.$output}}\n- `ExpenseReports`: {{$context.$nodes.GETEXPENSEREPORTS.$output}}\n- `ISRs`: {{$context.$nodes.GETINTERNALSERVICEREQUEST.$output}}\n\n### Instructions\nReturn up to maximum 5 items from all available data using the priority order below.\n\n#### Selection Rules (STRICT)\n1. Use this exact priority order:\n   - Priority 1: `SRs` and `ISRs` with severity `Very High` or `High`\n   - Priority 2: `Absences`\n   - Priority 3: `ExpenseReports`\n   - Priority 4: remaining `SRs` and `ISRs` with other severities such as `Medium` or `Low`\n2. Start with Priority 1 and add items until you reach 5 items or Priority 1 is exhausted.\n3. If fewer than 5 items are selected after Priority 1, continue filling remaining slots using Priority 2, then Priority 3, then Priority 4.\n4. Never exceed 5 items in total.\n5. If multiple items qualify within the same priority level, select the most recently updated or submitted ones first.\n6. Do not skip available Priority 1 `SRs` or `ISRs` in favor of `Absences` or `ExpenseReports`.\n7. Do not invent missing values. If a value is empty, omit that part of the text.\n\n---\n\n**ROOT CONFIGURATION:** \n1. `title`: Generate a concise headline (e.g., \"Requests waiting for review or approval\"). \n2. `description`: Generate a short, non-repetitive summary of the available data.\n\n---\n\n**STRICT MAPPING RULES:**\n\n1. `items[].subTitle`:\n   - For `SRs` and `ISRs` - map the `SrNumber`\n   - For `Absences` - map `SubmitDate` and mention `Submitted on <SubmitDate>`. If `SubmitDate` is empty, don't mention it.\n   - For `ExpenseReports` - map `purpose`. If `purpose` is empty, don't mention it.\n\n2. `items[].summary`:\n   - For `SRs` and `ISRs` - map the short summary of problem description and `messageContent` of `ora_svc_customer_entry` in less than 100 words.\n   - Treat the user as the customer.\n   - Refer to the customer as `you`.\n   - Maintain a neutral, third-person summarizer tone.\n   - For `Absences` - map `formattedDuration`, `startDate`, `EndDate` and mention `<formattedDuration> from <startDate> to <EndDate>`. If any values are empty, don't mention them.\n   - For `ExpenseReports` - map `ReportSubmitDate` by saying `Expense Report submitted on <ReportSubmitDate> is waiting for approval.` If any values are empty, don't mention them.\n\n3. `items[].priority`:\n   - For `SRs` and `ISRs` - map the severity:\n     - use `\"alert\"` for `Very High` or `High`\n     - otherwise use `\"warning\"`\n   - For `Absences` and `ExpenseReports` - use `\"warning\"`\n\n4. `items[].timestamp`:\n   - For `SRs` - set as `\"Help Desk Request\"`\n   - For `ISRs` - set as `\"Internal Help Desk Request\"`\n   - For `Absences` - set as `\"Leave of Absence\"`\n   - For `ExpenseReports` - set as `\"Expense Report\"`\n\n5. `items[].additionalAction`:\n    - For Absence - set it as {\"text\": \"Send follow-up\", \"command\": \"ora.Agent({\\\"action\\\": \\\"ManagerApproval\\\", \\\"expenseReportNumber\\\" : \"<absenceType>\"})\"}\n    - For Expense Report - set it as {\"text\": \"Send follow-up\", \"command\": \"ora.Agent({\\\"action\\\": \\\"ManagerApproval\\\", \\\"expenseReportNumber\\\" : \"<ExpenseReportNumber>\"})\"}\n\n6. `items[].title`:\n   - For `SRs` and `ISRs` - map the `Title`\n   - For `Absences` - map the `absenceType`\n   - For `ExpenseReports` - map the `ExpenseReportNumber`\n\n7. `items[].badge`:\n   - For `SRs` and `ISRs` - map the `StatusTypeCdMeaning`\n   - For `Absences` - map the `absenceDispStatusMeaning`\n   - For `ExpenseReports` - set as `Pending Approval`\n\n### Output Rules\n1. Do not return markdown.\n2. Do not include explanations.\n3. Preserve the selected item order based on the priority rules above.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
